  "n-canvas": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 1400,
   "text": "The canvas stays the base: pages and an outline in a rail, sections with readable labels, a map, fit and 1:1, an inspector for the selected board. Render (voice, scheme, pen) is chosen once for every board, by picture.",
   "page": "canvas"
  },
  "n-review": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 1400,
   "text": "The lead: a proposal is reviewed board by board. The changed boards with “seen” (kept in the browser), before and after in four ways, in any state; the matrix shows one board in every voice and scheme, with the contrast check’s failures marked.",
   "page": "review"
  },
  "n-board": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 1400,
   "text": "One board on the desk with its states as a filmstrip ($states, see Start here › Convention), and on the device in e-ink. The flow is drawn from links and states and can be walked step by step.",
   "page": "board"
  },
  "n-parts": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 1400,
   "text": "The components the boards above are made of. Thumb is a schematic screen that follows the voice and scheme; the mockups use it in place of real boards, which a design folder cannot import from another.",
